From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LinearMC <linearmc@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 29 Sep 2026 00:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Linear core decoupling: NMS-free net.linear boundary

Decouples the Linear core from NMS so common/linear-core compiles standalone:
opaque ChunkKey longs replace ChunkPos at the AbstractRegionFile boundary
(exact slot math, vanilla log format preserved), Paper-config reads become
adapter-registered suppliers (runtime-reload semantics kept), the flush bridge
becomes a no-op-default listener, and conversion storage opens become an
injected RegionOpener (probe default handles LINEAR directly). RegionFile
gains long-key bridge overloads (vanilla ChunkPos bodies untouched);
RegionFileStorage/Upgrader convert at the boundary; the factory delegates
constants/clamp to core RegionFileFormat. Behavior-preserving: the full
LinearNmsTestSuite (119 tests) is green before and after.
